WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:17.621
Per cent means out of 100. To find a part as a percentage of a total, divide the part by the whole, then multiply by 100. Here, 5 circles out of 20 are coloured. 5 divided by 20, times 100, is 25 per cent.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:38.787
Percentages make a fair comparison when groups are different sizes. Class A has 6 left-handed pupils out of 20. Class B has 9 out of 40. B has more, but A has the bigger share: 30 per cent against 22.5 per cent. In a compare question, give both the numbers and the percentages.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:56.305
Step one. Find the part and the whole. This example table shows babies' birth mass. Its numbers are made up, not real data. The question asks: what percentage of babies born to non-smoking mothers had a low birth mass? The part is 20.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:13.796
Step two. The whole is the total for that group only: all babies born to non-smoking mothers. That is 210, not the grand total of 310. If no total is given, add up that row: 20 plus 190 is 210.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:28.985
Step three. Write part divided by whole, times 100. 20 divided by 210 is 0.0952. Times 100 is 9.52, so about 9.5 per cent.

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:38.681
Step four. Check. A part can never be more than 100 per cent of its own whole. Then round sensibly, often to one decimal place.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:56.227
Here is a real exam question. In one year in the United Kingdom there were 4733 organ donations. 3233 of them were kidney donations. Calculate the percentage that were kidney donations.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:09.195
The whole is all organ donations: 4733. The part is the kidney donations: 3233. So the kidney part of the bar is most of it.

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:28.673
Percentage equals 3233 divided by 4733, times 100. 3233 divided by 4733 is 0.683. Times 100 is 68.3 per cent.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:42.391
Check: 68.3 per cent is less than 100, and kidneys are most of the donations, about two thirds. So it makes sense. Explanation by olevels.com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:58.775
A common mistake is dividing the whole by the part: 4733 divided by 3233. That gives 146 per cent, which is impossible. The part always goes on top.

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:08.865
Another mistake is forgetting to multiply by 100, and writing 0.68 as the answer. That is a fraction, not a percentage.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:23.973
Your turn. In one month, 2400 people gave blood at a hospital. 864 of them had blood group O. Calculate the percentage of donors with blood group O. Pause here and work it out.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:32.289
The whole is all the donors: 2400. The part is the group O donors: 864.

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:47.698
864 divided by 2400 is 0.36. Times 100 is 36 per cent. Check: it is less than 100, and about a third of the bar. So 36 per cent.

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:57.743
So, every time: find the part. Find the whole for that group. Divide the part by the whole, times 100. Then check it is below 100.
